# Campaign (short), part "websocket", core steps only: every server as it is and with BEAM
# busy-waiting off, in one shuffled order. About 11 h instead of about 28 h.
#   make run CONFIG=campaigns/short/websocket-core.config
# Why fewer steps (2026-10-04): a WebSocket load lasts 1.5-5 s, while every measurement costs about
# a minute of fixed overhead (container start, readiness check, Scaphandre). Time therefore scales
# with the number of steps. Kept: one step per question, at the heavy end (100 clients):
#   - concurrency 100 / 1000 / 5000 clients: the BEAM's strength
#   - burst and stream with 100 clients, 8 KB and 1 MB messages
#   - payload sweep with 5 clients up to 64 MB: the large-payload case from Erlang '26
# Dropped: 5 and 50 clients in burst and stream, and 64 MB with many clients (minutes per step).
# Same as the other parts: 5 repeats, no idle measurement (an idle server draws 0.1-2 mW).
MACHINE=minimal
MEASURE=websocket concurrency payload
VARIANTS=nobw:ERL_FLAGS=+sbwt none +sbwtdcpu none +sbwtdio none
REPEATS=5
IDLE_SECONDS=0
WS_BURST_CLIENTS=100
WS_BURST_SIZES_KB=8 1024
WS_STREAM_CLIENTS=100
WS_STREAM_SIZES_KB=8 1024
WS_CONCURRENCY_CLIENTS=100 1000 5000
WS_PAYLOAD_CLIENTS=5
WS_PAYLOAD_SIZES_KB=8 1024 65536
